description=Only for loading a save that has no player 3 in it: player 3 joins as a new Allessia instead of a copy of player 2. New games ignore this - pick Three Player in the menu.
patch=0,EE,000A1BE8,word,50330009

[P3 character - Drizzt]
author=H + Claude
description=Only for loading a save that has no player 3 in it: player 3 joins as a new Drizzt instead of a copy of player 2. New games ignore this - pick Three Player in the menu.
patch=0,EE,000A1BE8,word,50330004

[P3 character - Artemis]
author=H + Claude
description=Only for loading a save that has no player 3 in it: player 3 joins as a new Artemis instead of a copy of player 2. New games ignore this - pick Three Player in the menu.
patch=0,EE,000A1BE8,word,5033000A

[P3 character - Vahn (DA1 hero, test)]
author=H + Claude
description=TEST. Whenever a new player 3 is created (a Three Player new game, whatever player 3 picks on the character screen, or a save without player 3) player 3 is the human archer of Dark Alliance 1 (needs the updated 3P ISO: run make_3p_iso.bat again). A save that already has a player 3 keeps that character.
patch=0,EE,000A1BE8,word,50340001

[P3 character - Adrianna (DA1 hero, test)]
author=H + Claude
description=TEST. Whenever a new player 3 is created (a Three Player new game, whatever player 3 picks on the character screen, or a save without player 3) player 3 is the elven sorceress of Dark Alliance 1. A save that already has a player 3 keeps that character.
patch=0,EE,000A1BE8,word,50340002

[P3 character - Kromlech (DA1 hero, test)]
author=H + Claude
description=TEST. Whenever a new player 3 is created (a Three Player new game, whatever player 3 picks on the character screen, or a save without player 3) player 3 is the dwarven fighter of Dark Alliance 1 (needs the updated 3P ISO: run make_3p_iso.bat again). A save that already has a player 3 keeps that character.
patch=0,EE,000A1BE8,word,50340003

[DA1 heroes - shouts kept in sound memory]
author=H + Claude
description=Only if the streamed shouts ever bother you. Vahn / Adrianna / Kromlech normally have their shouts (special moves, casting) streamed from the disc like their spoken lines, one voice at a time. With this ticked the shouts are kept in sound memory again (they can overlap with spoken lines), which costs about 46 KB of the 2 MB sound memory per DA1 hero, so fewer creature sounds fit. Takes effect after a restart of the game.
patch=0,EE,000A1FA4,word,53440002

[TEST - all players always have 200 feat points]
author=H + Claude
description=TEST ONLY. Lets every player buy every feat at once so each one can be tried. Untick it again afterwards (the points a character has at that moment stay in the save).
patch=1,EE,000B00E0,word,000000C8
patch=1,EE,000B6410,word,000000C8
patch=1,EE,000BC740,word,000000C8

[TEST - party always has 500000 gold]
author=H + Claude
description=TEST ONLY. For buying weapons and armour to try (e.g. a warhammer for Kromlech, or the random shop stock). Untick it again afterwards (build 49: raised from 50000).
patch=1,EE,000B00DC,word,0007A120

[TEST - Trade Way goblins with player spells]
author=H + Claude
description=TEST ONLY (build 47). On the Trade Way the first three goblins after the caravan guard get player abilities: a goblin archer whose arrows are Shock Arrows, an axe goblin that fires Repulsion with about a third of its swings (it now knocks the players down and slides them back), and a goblin shaman who casts Ball Lightning. Everything else is unchanged. Needs a restart of the game; works on a saved game too (the goblins are made when the level loads).
patch=0,EE,000AC000,word,00000001
